{"name":"Family Tree","hex":"#a7b191","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"family tree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A diagrammatic representation of a pedigree, illustrating the connections between a person's ancestors, offspring and other relatives.","The totality of someone's ancestors and offspring."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/family_tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Family tree","blocks":[{"text":"A family tree, also called a genealogical tree or a pedigree chart, is a chart representing family relationships in a conventional tree structure. More detailed family trees, used in medicine and social work, are known as genograms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Family_tree.svg/330px-Family_tree.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Family_tree","wikidata":"Q189977"},{"title":"Family","blocks":[{"text":"Family is a group of people related either by consanguinity or affinity. It forms the basis for social order. Ideally, families offer predictability, structure, and safety as members mature and learn to participate in the community. Historically, most human societies use family as the primary purpose of attachment, nurturance, and socialization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Sauk_Indian_family_by_Frank_Rinehart_1899.jpg/330px-Sauk_Indian_family_by_Frank_Rinehart_1899.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Family","wikidata":"Q8436"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Emma_%26_Carl_J._Sandberg_family_tree.jpg/500px-Emma_%26_Carl_J._Sandberg_family_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Emma_%26_Carl_J._Sandberg_family_tree.jpg/1280px-Emma_%26_Carl_J._Sandberg_family_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Emma_%26_Carl_J._Sandberg_family_tree.jpg/500px-Emma_%26_Carl_J._Sandberg_family_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Three generations of ancestors (born from 1824 to 1916)[1] placed on a Swedish kurbits tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmma_%26_Carl_J._Sandberg_family_tree.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Waldburg_Ahnentafel.jpg/500px-Waldburg_Ahnentafel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Waldburg_Ahnentafel.jpg/500px-Waldburg_Ahnentafel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An ahnentafel family tree displaying an ancestor chart of Sigmund Christoph, Graf von Zeil und Trauchburg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWaldburg_Ahnentafel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Family_Tree_Sample.jpg/500px-Family_Tree_Sample.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"h